STEP 3 — Backend Python packages

What I did (installed inside backend/venv):
- fastapi                 0.143.3   -> web framework for the API
- uvicorn                 0.54.0    -> server that runs FastAPI
- python-dotenv           1.2.4     -> reads settings from the .env file
- google-generativeai     0.8.6     -> Google Gemini AI SDK
- mysql-connector-python  26.7.0    -> connects Python to MySQL

Then I saved the full list of installed packages to:
    backend/requirements.txt

How to reinstall everything later:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r backend\requirements.txt

Note:
- Google now also offers a newer SDK called "google-genai". We used
  "google-generativeai" as requested; it installs and works fine on Python 3.13.
